  "description": "Subject: Remediation Guidance \u2013 Vulnerability Rating Taxonomy Mapping  \n\nPlease find below the current remediation advice linked to our vulnerability rating taxonomy entries, along with the reference sources for each recommendation. No generic default advice is defined; each item includes its own specific guidance and supporting documentation.\n\n- **Weak Passwords** (ID:\u202fweak_passwords) \u2013 Enforce strong password policies and enable multi\u2011factor authentication. For detailed guidelines see\u202fhttps://example.com/password\u2011guidelines\u202fand the NIST specification at\u202fhttps://nist.gov/800-63.  \n- **Network Vulnerability** (ID:\u202fnetwork_vulnerability) comprises two sub\u2011issues:  \n  \u2022 **Open Ports** (ID:\u202fopen_ports) \u2013 Close unnecessary ports and restrict access via firewall rules. Reference:\u202fhttps://example.com/ports.  \n  \u2022 **Unpatched Services** (ID:\u202funpatched_services) \u2013 Apply the latest security patches to all services. Reference:\u202fhttps://securityupdates.example.com."
